    "done_when": "Write the tangent of every complete-elliptic and harmonic-moment recurrence the Biot point jet differentiates as its own recurrence, the first family of the lead's locked custom-derivative-rules decision. Context (derivative-rules probe, run r-20261006T015404732285): autodiff of the point jet's field rows is pathological for XLA, one tangent direction does not compile in 420 s on CPU where the primal compiles in 23.5 s, and nova/biot has no analytic second-derivative kernel, so the rule is derived through the recurrences. Scope: nova/biot/elliptic.py and nova/biot/completeelliptic.py only; the functions the point jet reaches there, which the node enumerates first from the jaxpr of packed_analytic_moments (expected: complete_kind, complete_pole, harmonic_moments, harmonic_pole_moments, harmonic_root_moments and their paired forms where the jet uses them, and the descent and accumulation helpers beneath them). Done when: (1) for each such function F a private tangent function computes the jvp of F with respect to all its floating inputs as its own recurrence or closed form (for example the classical derivatives of K and E in the parameter, carried through the same descent the primal uses), returning the same structure jax.jvp(F) returns, without calling jax.jvp, jax.grad or jax.jacfwd on F; (2) identity: on 10,000 random inputs spanning the domain the jet uses (near-singular parameters near 1 included), each tangent agrees with jax.jvp of the base F to relative 1e-13 per output, maxima printed; (3) negative control: each tangent with its recurrence truncated by one term fails that identity, maximum printed; (4) cold compile of each tangent against jax.jvp of the base F, in fresh cache-disabled CPU processes on all_debug, wall and expanded equations recorded, showing the tangent compiles no slower than the primal by more than a factor of three; (5) no change to any primal function's arithmetic (the primal outputs are bit-identical to the base, asserted), and the existing tests/biot suite and the elliptic tests pass by delta; (6) a test module tests/biot/test_elliptic_tangent_recurrences.py holding the identity, control and compile rows, and an evidence fragment docs/evidence/fragments/converged-forward-solve/cfs-elliptic-tangent-recurrences.html with plan-evidence-for converged-forward-solve, reckon audit-doc 0 errors. The custom_jvp wrapping of the point jet is a later node; this node does not wrap. Gates run on compute, never the login node: H200 jobs through RECKON_ALLOW_NESTED_LAUNCH=1 scripts/h200_test_lane/run.sh --log (an absolute path under the run directory named in the manifest) --wait -- (the targets of that step); CPU measurements on all_debug with srun (TMPDIR=/tmp, JAX_PLATFORMS=cpu, the shared interpreter /home/ITER/mcintos/Code/nova/.venv/bin/python run directly with PYTHONPATH set to the run worktree, orientation_worktree in the manifest, never uv on a compute node). Every cold compile runs in a fresh subprocess with the persistent compilation cache disabled in the environment before jax is imported, and asserts a cache miss from the guard rows. Any wait is declared with wait_probe sacct -n -X -P -j (job id) -o State and wait_terminal COMPLETED FAILED CANCELLED TIMEOUT OUT_OF_MEMORY NODE_FAIL, never exit:0. Every login-node uv command carries --no-sync and nothing runs uv sync; configure_dtypes() before any array and jax_enable_x64 asserted True. Base-revision code is loaded through importlib from git show at the run orientation_base_sha under a different module name, never copied into the tree. No public signature changes. Figures, if any, go under docs/figures/kernel-derivative-rules. Commit with conventional subjects and bodies at every step and write the manifest before every job wait; the manifest commits line lists every commit.",
